{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner decision on 2b33f44d, the default-room limit. My survey 579ba80d said no question was open, and it missed this one.\n\nLand the Page head as it stands, and do not restart its gate for this. J5's scene runs on a room with the Brief definition, so the limit does not touch that run.\n\nThen change the behaviour, under J5's leftovers e82c6550. \"Could not read\" must mean that a read failed. A lane whose definition this list does not model did not fail. On a default room, every lane says it failed today, on the first screen, and a person learns to ignore it, which also hides a real failure. So:\n1. Keep two groups. A read that failed keeps the current words and stays at the top.\n2. A lane under a definition the list does not model goes below the list, collapsed, with words such as \"This list covers questions and approvals. 3 lanes use other rules. Open each one to see what it asks.\" State plainly that the list can leave out items there.\n3. A person with an empty list on a default room must see that nothing in the list needs them, and that the list did not cover those lanes.\n\nThis stays honest and stops being noisy. A generic list across any definition is a later design, and not part of this.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}